tion and equestrian sites, in a Joshua tree forest south of Yucca Valley; reservations up to 6 months ahead"},{"name":"Indian Cove Campground (NPS)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/campgrounds.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","group","family"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov, 1-877-444-6777","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"101 sites at 3,200 ft west of Twentynine Palms, $35/night, no water, with group sites; access to the Wonderland of Rocks; reservations up to 6 months ahead"},{"name":"Cottonwood Campground (NPS)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/campgrounds.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","group"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov, 1-877-444-6777","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"62 sites at 3,000 ft near the South Entrance, $35/night, water and flush toilets, tent-only group sites; named by the NPS for darker skies; reservations up to 6 months ahead"},{"name":"Hidden Valley Campground (NPS, first-come)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/campgrounds.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","sports"],"booking_route":"first-come, first-served - no reservations","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"44 first-come sites at 4,200 ft, $25/night, open year-round; occupy an empty site, then register and pay at an entrance station within one hour"},{"name":"Joshua Tree Lake RV & Campground","source":"https://www.joshuatreelake.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","group"],"booking_route":"own site, Hipcamp, or Spot2Nite; walk-ins accepted","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"family-owned at 2601 Sunfair Road, 2,300 ft, with full-hookup RV sites, dry camping, tent sites, hot showers and a dump station; hosts meteor gazing events; fishing currently closed for maintenance"},{"name":"Joshua Tree RV & Campground","source":"https://jtrvcamp.com","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","group"],"booking_route":"Campspot","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"\"the only RV Park in Downtown Joshua Tree\", 6225 Sunburst St, with restrooms, showers and the only campground laundry in town by its own account"},{"name":"Desert Drifter RV Resort, Yucca Valley","source":"https://www.desertdrifterrv.com","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["glamping","family"],"booking_route":"Campspot","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"25 x 80 ft full-hookup big-rig sites plus fully furnished vintage travel trailers, heated pool and sauna, at 55408 Twentynine Palms Highway"},{"name":"Twentynine Palms RV Resort","source":"https://www.twentyninepalmsresort.com","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["senior","family"],"booking_route":"own website; phone (760) 367-3320","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"full-service RV sites and cottages at 4949 Desert Knoll Avenue with clubhouse, pool, spa and laundry"},{"name":"Pioneertown Corrals Camping","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/california-pioneertown-corrals-camping-ozxhknrl","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","group","culture"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"63 sites on 6 acres - tent, RV and horse sites with 17 corrals, no hookups or potable water - behind Mane Street, Pappy & Harriet''s and the Red Dog Saloon"},{"name":"Palm Springs/Joshua Tree KOA, Desert Hot Springs","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/camping-outside-of-the-park.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family"],"booking_route":"not observed (koa.com returned 403)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"named by the NPS among private campgrounds south of the park, at 70405 Dillon Road, Desert Hot Springs"},{"name":"BLM dispersed camping north and south of the park","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/camping-outside-of-the-park.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["expedition","adventure"],"booking_route":"not applicable - no booking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"two mapped areas on Bureau of Land Management land beside the park boundary with \"no restrooms, no water, no trash collection\""},{"name":"Cliffhanger Guides, Joshua Tree","source":"https://www.cliffhangerguides.com/book-your-trip/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"request form, email or phone 760-401-5033 - no automated engine","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"owner-operated at 6551 Park Blvd - rock climbing, \"deserteering\", hiking and 3-day climbing courses for ages 3-103; states it is \"legally permitted and insured to operate within Joshua Tree National Park\"; half day from $150/person (5+) to $315 solo"},{"name":"Vertical Adventures, Joshua Tree","source":"https://www.verticaladventures.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","sports"],"booking_route":"own online reservation form (engine not named); (760) 705-8994","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"AMGA-certified climbing school since 1983 at 60175 La Mirada Trail - beginner to lead and self-rescue courses, small groups, half and full days seven days a week"},{"name":"Desert Institute (Joshua Tree National Park Association)","source":"https://www.joshuatree.org/desert-institute/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","senior","group","wildlife"],"booking_route":"Humanitix (classes); private tours via its own request page","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"the park''s nonprofit partner since 1962 runs seasonal field classes on ecology, art and history, private naturalist-led tours and step-on bus tours, plus the park''s visitor center stores"},{"name":"Big Wheel Tours, Palm Desert and Palm Springs","source":"https://www.bwbtours.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["senior","family","group"],"booking_route":"Peek (peek.com)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"since 1998 - Joshua Tree off-road and driving tours from $199 per person by SUV, plus bike tours and rentals"},{"name":"Desert Adventures Red Jeep Tours, Palm Desert","source":"https://www.red-jeep.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["group","family","senior"],"booking_route":"FareHarbor","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"a 6-hour Joshua Tree walking/hiking excursion with hotel pickup, \"$1,890 per vehicle\", Monday to Friday"},{"name":"Joshua Tree Outfitters","source":"https://www.joshuatreeoutfitters.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"phone/email/text only - 760-366-1848","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"camping and climbing gear rental in downtown Joshua Tree at 61707 29 Palms Highway - tents, sleeping bags, stoves, coolers, bouldering pads, guidebooks"},{"name":"Sky''s The Limit Observatory and Nature Center, Twentynine Palms","source":"https://www.skysthelimit29.org","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","culture","romance"],"booking_route":"Humanitix for festival tickets; programs listed on own site","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"a volunteer-run nonprofit at 9697 Utah Trail with monthly programs and stargazing through volunteer telescopes, including a dome-mounted scope"},{"name":"Night Sky Festival, October 9-10, 2026","source":"https://www.skysthelimit29.org/night-sky-festival","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["family","culture"],"booking_route":"Humanitix (events.humanitix.com/night-sky-festival)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"11th annual - telescope clinics, astronomy lectures, a new Family Space Camp and evening stargazing at Sky''s The Limit and Patriotic Hall, Twentynine Palms; co-hosted with the Joshua Tree National Park Association"},{"name":"The Integratron, Landers","source":"https://www.integratron.com/sound-bath","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wellness","culture","romance","group"],"booking_route":"own reservation calendar; private sessions by email; gift certificates via FareHarbor","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"60-minute quartz crystal singing bowl sound baths at 2477 Belfield Blvd - public sessions up to 33 people at $62.89 per person, private sessions $1,300-$2,000; open Wednesday to Saturday; closes January 3 to February 2, 2027"},{"name":"Pappy & Harriet''s, Pioneertown","source":"https://www.pappyandharriets.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","culinary","group","romance"],"booking_route":"not observed (site references Knitting Factory; ticket engine not named)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"\"Classic American fare amid rustic Western decor, plus extras including BBQ & live music\" at 53688 Pioneertown Road"},{"name":"Pioneertown Motel","source":"https://www.pioneertown-motel.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","romance"],"booking_route":"own website booking engine (not named); 760-365-7001","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"a boutique motel on historic Mane Street, 5240 Curtis Road, with the Pioneertown Mountains Preserve on its grounds and the Red Dog Saloon as sister venue; pets $50/night"},{"name":"Joshua Tree Music Festival, October 8-11, 2026","source":"https://joshuatreemusicfestival.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","family","wellness"],"booking_route":"Afton Tickets (aftontickets.com)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"the 21st fall festival - a family-friendly four-night campout with live music, movement, mindfulness and more than 100 workshops"},{"name":"Joshua Tree Retreat Center","source":"https://www.jtrcc.org/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wellness","group","culture"],"booking_route":"email/phone only - bookings.jtrc@gmail.com, 760-469-9764","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"\"the oldest and largest retreat center in the Western United States\" at 59700 29 Palms Highway, a National Historic Place since January 2023 with \"the largest collection of Lloyd Wright buildings in the country\"; retreats, workshops, breathwork"},{"name":"Noah Purifoy Outdoor Desert Art Museum, Joshua Tree","source":"https://www.noahpurifoy.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture"],"booking_route":"not applicable - free entry, no booking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"outdoor assemblage sculpture, open \"every day from dawn to dusk\", free, donations welcome"},{"name":"29 Palms Inn and the Oasis of Mara","source":"https://29palmsinn.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["romance","culture","culinary"],"booking_route":"Vertical Booking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"adobe bungalows and wood-framed cabins on 70 acres with \"the Oasis of Mara at its core\"; restaurant Wednesday to Sunday, working with Faultline Farm"},{"name":"Harmony Motel, Twentynine Palms","source":"https://www.harmonymotel.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culture","romance"],"booking_route":"ResNexus","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"a 1952 hilltop motel with pool, hot tub and the Jack Kerouac Cabin"},{"name":"Sacred Sands, Joshua Tree","source":"https://www.sacredsands.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["romance","wellness"],"booking_route":"own engine (booknow.sacredsands.com)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"a boutique hotel and wedding venue with two couples'' rooms with private patios and soaking tub, plus the Lobo Luna House for four"},{"name":"Homestead Modern, Yucca Valley","source":"https://homesteadmodern.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["group","romance","family"],"booking_route":"own integrated booking engine (not named); partners with Kind Traveler","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"60+ curated design homes and cabins across Joshua Tree, Pioneertown and Yucca Valley since 2010, including The Bungalows at the Joshua Tree Retreat Center with ADA units"},{"name":"Joshua Tree Saloon & Grill","source":"https://www.joshuatreesaloon.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","culture","group"],"booking_route":"not observed - no reservation route on its site","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"since 1984 at 61835 Twentynine Palms Highway - the Mineshaft Burger and live music on the patio Friday to Sunday"},{"name":"Crossroads Cafe, Joshua Tree","source":"https://www.crossroadscafejtree.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"not observed - no reservation route on its site","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"a from-scratch diner at 61715 29 Palms Hwy - pancakes, burgers, fish tacos, chorizo and egg, beer and wine - open daily 7:30 am to 2:30 pm"},{"name":"La Copine, Yucca Valley (Flamingo Heights)","source":"https://www.lacopinekitchen.com/info","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"text-only reservations to 760-289-8537, up to four weeks ahead; walk-ins welcome","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"\"New California\" cooking by Claire Wadsworth and Nikki Hill at 848 Old Woman Springs Rd - a New York Times Critic''s Pick, with its own cookbook; Thursday to Sunday, 11 am to 4 pm"},{"name":"Shields Date Garden, Indio","source":"https://www.shieldsdategarden.com/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","family","senior"],"booking_route":"online shop for products; cafe walk-in (no reservation route observed)","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"a date farm and shop open since December 24, 1924 - Medjool, Deglet Noor and Barhi dates, Date Crystals, fresh citrus - with The Cafe at Shields (8 am to 2 pm daily per its site) and a garden walk"},{"name":"29 Palms Certified Farmers Market","source":"https://visit29.org/","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["culinary","family","culture"],"booking_route":"not applicable - no booking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"listed by the Twentynine Palms visitors bureau for October 3 at 73551 29 Palms Highway"},{"name":"Pioneertown Mountains Preserve and Big Morongo Canyon Preserve","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/nearbyattractions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02","si":["wildlife","hiking"],"booking_route":"not applicable - no booking","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","blurb":"two preserves on the NPS Nearby Attractions list - Pioneertown Mountains Preserve (Wildlands Conservancy) and Big Morongo Canyon Preserve, Morongo Valley"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is there lodging or food inside Joshua Tree National Park?","a":"No. The NPS states there is no lodging in the park, and no gas stations, restaurants or grocery stores. There is no water in the interior of the park, so visitors bring their own food, water and supplies.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/basicinfo.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"How do I book a campsite in Joshua Tree?","a":"Black Rock, Cottonwood, Indian Cove, Jumbo Rocks, Ryan and Sheep Pass Group take reservations on recreation.gov the same day or up to 6 months ahead. Belle, Hidden Valley and White Tank are first-come, first-served: occupy a site, then register and pay at an entrance station within one hour.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/campgrounds.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"How much does it cost to enter Joshua Tree?","a":"$30 per private vehicle for 7 days, $25 per motorcycle, $15 per person on foot or bicycle (under 16 free), or $55 for a Joshua Tree Annual Pass.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Do non-US residents pay the $100 nonresident fee at Joshua Tree?","a":"The NPS list of parks charging a $100 nonresident fee to non-US residents 16 and over names eleven parks, and Joshua Tree is not on it.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/aboutus/entrance-fee-prices.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"When is Joshua Tree busiest?","a":"October through May, with the busiest times on weekends, holidays and spring break (March to mid-April). The NPS suggests arriving before 8 am and using the North or South Entrance; the West Entrance is the busiest.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/visiting-during-the-busy-season.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"},{"q":"Where is the best stargazing in Joshua Tree?","a":"The park is an International Dark Sky Park with designated stargazing areas at Quail Springs, Hidden Valley, Cap Rock and Ryan Mountain parking lots; for darker skies the NPS names Cottonwood Campground and Pinto Basin Road between Cholla Cactus Garden and Cottonwood.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/jotr/planyourvisit/stargazing.htm","accessed":"2026-10-02"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Joshua Tree National Park: Climbing, Dark Skies & Pioneertown | TravelWell","meta_description":"How Joshua Tree''s campgrounds book, when the crowds come, where to see the stars, and where to stay from AutoCamp''s Airstreams to Pioneertown.","slug":"joshua-tree-national-park-california","primary_keyword":"Joshua Tree National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Joshua Tree National Park, California"}}'::jsonb, 89)
