  ('kings-canyon-california', '12A', 'Kings Canyon National Park', 'United States', 'General Grant Tree and the glaciated Cedar Grove canyon', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Central Coast & the Sierra', '{"hiking","adventure","family","group","parks"}', '{"dramatic","rugged","wild"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"General Grant Tree Trail","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/ggdayhikesum.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail; park entrance fee applies","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"A \"1/3 mile (0.5 km)\" \"paved trail\": \"One of the world''s largest living trees. President Coolidge proclaimed it the Nation''s Christmas tree in 1926.\" The NPS calls the tree \"the world''s second largest tree by volume\". Joint SEKI page; the tree is in Kings Canyon''s Grant Grove."},{"name":"Zumwalt Meadow Trail","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cgdayhikesum.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"\"0.8 mile (1.3 km)\" that \"passes high granite walls, lush meadows, and the Kings River\"; \"relatively level and may be suitable for some wheelchair users.\" Cedar Grove, Kings Canyon side (joint SEKI page)."},{"name":"Mist Falls Trail","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cgdayhikesum.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"An \"8-mile round trip\" from Cedar Grove: a \"sandy trail follows the glaciated South Fork Canyon through forest and chaparral\", gaining \"600''\" \"during the last mile.\""},{"name":"Roaring River Falls","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cgdayhikesum.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"\"A very short, shady walk to a powerful waterfall rushing through a granite chute\"; \"Paved, relatively accessible.\" The planner lists it at 0.4 miles from a trailhead on Highway 180."},{"name":"Panoramic Point","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/grant-grove.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - park viewpoint","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"\"offering great views of the Kings Canyon, Hume Lake, and the mountains beyond\"; the trail is 0.5 miles from the Panoramic Point parking lot (spring planner). \"Motor homes and trailers prohibited\" on the road, which the planner lists among spring closures."},{"name":"Big Stump Loop Trail","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/ggdayhikesum.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","culture","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"A \"2-mile loop\" \"through an old-growth giant sequoia grove that was logged in the late nineteenth century\", with \"large sequoia stumps\" (the spring planner gives 1.6 miles from the Big Stump Picnic Area). Big Stump is \"The first resting spot after the park entrance station on Highway 180\"."},{"name":"North Grove Loop","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/ggdayhikesum.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"\"1.5 mile (2.4 km)\", \"lightly traveled\", with \"a close look at the big trees\" through \"meadows and creeks, through mixed conifer and sequoia forest\"."},{"name":"Big Baldy Ridge and Buena Vista Peak","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/ggdayhikesum.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"Big Baldy Ridge: \"roundtrip 4.4 miles (7.1 km)\", \"600 feet (183 m)\", \"great views out and down into Redwood Canyon\" to \"the summit at 8209 feet\". Buena Vista Peak: \"2 mile (3.2 km) round-trip\" to a \"360-degree view\"."},{"name":"Knapp''s Cabin and Sheep Creek Cascade","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cgdayhikesum.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","culture"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"Knapp''s Cabin: \"A short walk\" to a historic fishing cabin from the 1920s. Sheep Creek Cascade: a \"two-mile round trip\" that \"gains 600'' in elevation\" on a \"moderately strenuous hike up the forested Don Cecil Trail\"."},{"name":"Kings Canyon Visitor Center","source":"https://nps.gov/seki/learn/news/upload/Trip_Planner_2026_Spring_2026-03-19_01_for_web_508.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - free visitor center inside the fee area","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"Grant Grove: open \"9 am to 4:30 pm\" (spring 2026 planner); Park Store (Sequoia Parks Conservancy), \"Free public Wi-Fi\", \"Self-issue wilderness permits\"; manual wheelchairs to borrow; \"assistive listening devices and audio description are available for the park film.\""},{"name":"Wilderness permits from Roads End","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/wilderness_permits.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov (Sequoia and Kings Canyon National Parks Wilderness Permits) or self-issue station","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"\"Reservations can be made up to six months in advance of your trip, and are released daily at 7:00 AM Pacific Standard Time\"; 2026 quota season \"May 22, 2026 - September 26, 2026\"; \"$15 each trip plus $5 per person within the quota season\"; the Road''s End Permit Station in Cedar Grove opens \"7:00am - 3:30pm\" in quota season. The parks are \"97% designated Wilderness\" (spring planner)."},{"name":"Azalea Campground, Grant Grove","source":"https://www.recreation.gov/api/camps/campgrounds/10124502","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov or (877) 444-6777; off-season scan-and-pay in the Recreation.gov app","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"Recreation.gov: \"110 sites\" at 6,500 feet, each with \"a picnic table, a fire ring, and a food storage box\", flush toilets and potable water, near Grant Grove Village; \"Late spring, summer and early fall the campground is on reservations. When it is not on reservations sites are first come first served\". Planner: \"$32 per night\"."},{"name":"Sheep Creek Campground, Cedar Grove","source":"https://www.recreation.gov/api/camps/campgrounds/10044765","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking","motoring"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov or (877) 444-6777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"\"nestled in the stunning Kings Canyon, one of the deepest canyons in the United States\" and \"a wonderful place for families to spend time in the great outdoors\"; paved roads \"making it easier for both RVs and smaller cars\"; five comfort stations with flush toilets; the Cedar Grove Visitor Center is \".25 miles\" away."},{"name":"Moraine and Sentinel Campgrounds, Cedar Grove","source":"https://www.recreation.gov/api/camps/campgrounds/10044761","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","motoring"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov or (877) 444-6777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"Moraine: each site has \"a fire ring, picnic table and large bear-proof food storage box\", paved roads for RVs and cars, \"five comfort stations\"; Cedar Grove Visitor Center \".75 miles\" away. Sentinel: \"Each campsite has a large food storage locker (47\"W x 33\"D x 28\"H)\" (nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/sentinel.htm)."},{"name":"Canyon View Group Sites, Cedar Grove","source":"https://www.recreation.gov/api/camps/campgrounds/234753","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov or (877) 444-6777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"\"four large group sites and 12 mid-sized group sites for a total of 16 sites\"; \"This is a TENT ONLY Group Campground. No RV''s or Trailers allowed.\" Flush toilets and drinking water; \"Nearby the Kings River offers excellent trout fishing.\""},{"name":"Sunset Campground group sites, Grant Grove","source":"https://www.recreation.gov/api/camps/campgrounds/234752","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","hiking"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov or (877) 444-6777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"At 6,500 feet; \"Group sites A & B are for tents only\"; \"Each group site can accommodate 15-30 people\"; \"located across the street from Grant Grove Village\"; trails within walking distance include \"the one mile trail to the General Grant Tree\"."},{"name":"Grant Grove Stables","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/horseride.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","adventure"],"booking_route":"call the stable for reservations (number not on the NPS page); visitsequoia.com lists (866) 807-3598","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"\"1-2 hour guided trips. Routes include the General Grant Tree, North Grove, Lion Meadow, and Dead Giant Loop.\" \"Currently rides are offered to single family groups of up to 6 people.\" \"Open typically June through mid-October, weather permitting\". A concession permit holder."},{"name":"Cedar Grove Pack Station","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/horseride.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family"],"booking_route":"call the pack station; walk-in may be available for day rides","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"\"Rides range from one hour to all day, and there are options for all experience levels. Day trips offer rides along the Kings Canyon River.\" Single family groups of up to 6; \"Walk-in reservations may be available for day rides.\" June to mid-October."},{"name":"John Muir Lodge, Grant Grove","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/stay/lodging/john-muir-lodge/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","romance"],"booking_route":"own website (Synxis booking engine) or (866) 807-3598","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"\"The pinnacle of Kings Canyon lodging\", 36 rooms, \"Built in 1998\" with \"open-beam ceilings, a stone fireplace, and a historic redwood mantel\"; 86728 Highway 180; dogs at \"$25 per night\". Operated by DNC Parks & Resorts at SEKI, Inc. (Delaware North), the joint Sequoia and Kings Canyon concessioner."},{"name":"Grant Grove Cabins","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/stay/lodging/grant-grove-cabins/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","romance","group"],"booking_route":"own website (Synxis booking engine) or (866) 807-3598","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"\"both timber and tent cabin styles\": Duplex Cabin with Bath, Camp Cabin, Tent Cabin (\"Tent cabins do not have heat or electricity\") and the Honeymoon Cabin #9, \"Built in 1910\"; all \"within walking distance of Grant Grove and the world-famous General Grant Tree.\" Check-in at John Muir Lodge (Delaware North)."},{"name":"Cedar Grove Lodge","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/stay/lodging/cedar-grove-lodge/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"own website (Synxis booking engine) or (866) 807-3598","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"\"Nestled in a glaciated canyon, Cedar Grove Lodge is located in the heart of Kings Canyon National Park at Cedar Grove\"; \"Open May through mid-October\"; 21 rooms, Patio Rooms with a kitchenette; \"The front office at Cedar Grove Lodge closes daily at 9 p.m.\" (Delaware North)."},{"name":"Grant Grove Restaurant","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/kings-canyon-dining/grant-grove-restaurant/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in (no reservation method on the page)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"\"locally sourced, sustainable, and organic ingredients, surrounded by majestic giant sequoia trees overlooking Bradley Meadow\"; breakfast 7-10 a.m., lunch/dinner 11:30 a.m.-8 p.m.; a courtyard with seasonal walk-up pizza, sandwiches, coffee and ice cream; kids menu. 83923 CA-180."},{"name":"Cedar Grove Grill","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/kings-canyon-dining/cedar-grove-grill/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in counter service","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"\"light meals and snacks\" with \"outdoor al fresco dining on our balcony overlooking the Kings River\"; \"counter service\"; breakfast 7-10 AM, lunch 11:30 AM-2:30 PM, dinner 4-8 PM."},{"name":"Grant Grove Market","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/shop/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in store","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","gear","shop"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"\"Next to John Muir Lodge three miles from the Kings Canyon, Big Stump entrance\", \"a buzzing retail hub where visitors can resupply, reenergize and regroup on arrival\": groceries, beer, wine and camping supplies; in winter it stocks tire chains, hats and gloves, with snowshoes for rent. 9 AM-5 PM."},{"name":"Cedar Grove Market","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/shop/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking"],"booking_route":"walk-in store","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","eat","shop"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"\"near Roads End, right on Highway 180, for a fantastic park essentials pit stop\"; stocks camping gear, \"bear-proof food containers\", picnic supplies and souvenirs; 7 AM-9 PM. The NPS notes canister rental is available at visitor centers \"except for Cedar Grove\", so this is Cedar Grove''s canister source."},{"name":"Bear canister for the Rae Lakes Loop and Kings Canyon wilderness","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/bear_bc.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to bearvault.com (AvantLink); or rent at a park visitor center","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":8,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"NPS: \"Containers are required in the Dusy Basin, Rae Lakes Loop, North Dome, Rock Creek and Pear and Emerald Lakes areas from May 1 through October 31\"; rentals \"are available for rent at visitor centers, except for Cedar Grove\". The permit page adds that canisters \"are still required in most of the park, but may not be available for rental.\""},{"name":"Water filter for park streams","source":"https://nps.gov/seki/learn/news/upload/Trip_Planner_2026_Spring_2026-03-19_01_for_web_508.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"NPS: \"Park waterways may contain bacteria, including Giardia. Properly filter or treat water before drinking.\" And on altitude: \"Plan for a slow ascent and drink lots of water.\""},{"name":"Footwear traction and warm layers for snow season","source":"https://nps.gov/seki/learn/news/upload/Trip_Planner_2026_Spring_2026-03-19_01_for_web_508.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"The planner''s map legend: \"Traction device on footwear strongly recommended\" on winter routes; \"Hypothermia can occur year-round. Stay warm and eat snacks.\" Grant Grove Market stocks hats and gloves and rents snowshoes in winter (visitsequoia.com/shop)."},{"name":"Boyden Cavern","source":"https://boydencavern.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","group"],"booking_route":"FareHarbor (own website); walk-up tickets typically available in the mornings","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"\"a fantastic marble cavern\" with \"stalactites, stalagmites, flowstone, pendants, and shields\" in Sequoia National Forest, \"19 miles east of Grant Grove on Highway 180\"; walking tour 45-60 minutes, flashlight tours 65-75 minutes (minimum 4 guests); 2026 season \"7 days a week through Nov 8, 2026\"; \"a small family run business\" under a Forest Service permit."},{"name":"Kings River Expeditions","source":"https://www.kingsriver.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","group","river"],"booking_route":"FareHarbor (own website); Raft@KingsRiver.com","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"\"one and two-day whitewater rafting trips\" on \"the Class 3 Kings River\", \"just 90 minutes East of Fresno in the Sierra and Sequoia National Forests and near Kings Canyon and Yosemite National Parks\"; trips \"begin and end at Twin Pines Camp\"; group trips offered; next rafting season begins \"in April, 2027.\""},{"name":"Kings Canyon Scenic Byway (Highway 180)","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/byways.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","senior","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - public highway; park entrance fee applies inside the park","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["move"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"\"50 spectacular miles leading to Roads End, all along Highway 180\"; it \"begins in the foothills outside of Fresno\", \"enters the Grant Grove area of Kings Canyon National Park\", \"descends through Sequoia National Forest\" and \"ends at the Cedar Grove area\"."},{"name":"Hume Christian Camps, Hume Lake","source":"https://hume.org/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","pilgrimage","family"],"booking_route":"own registration portal (register.hume.org)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"\"Hume Christian Camps & Retreats\" at \"64144 Hume Lake Rd, Hume, CA 93628\": youth camps, adult retreats, school ministries and \"Guest group rentals\"; registration at register.hume.org. The NPS planner lists Hume Lake as the place to call for gas in Sequoia National Forest: \"Hume Lake (559) 305-7770\"."},{"name":"Mike And Di''s Retreat, Dunlap","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/california-mike-and-di-s-retreat-15-min-to-np-mxvhklkz","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","romance"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"Three \"Sky Pod\" tree-tent units on a 40-acre property near 5,000 feet, each sleeping 2, with \"Private flushing toilet and outdoor shower at each unit\", a shared outdoor kitchen and private decks; about 10-15 minutes from the Grant Grove Visitor Center (host)."},{"name":"Delilah Ridge Winery vintage glamping, Squaw Valley","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/california-delilah-ridge-winery-r57h5nrw","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","wine","romance"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","eat"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"\"46 acres\" with \"a small boutique winery\", wine tastings on site, and six vintage trailers and bell tents - \"Fiona (1967), Mai Tai (1954), Lola (1970 Airstream)\" - with electricity; a seasonal pool; \"only 20 minutes from the gates of Kings Canyon/Sequoia National Parks\" (host). Own site tagline: \"Your Kings Canyon & Sequoia Winery/Vintage Glamping Destination!\""},{"name":"Dunlap Canyon Retreat","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/california-dunlap-canyon-retreat-2ejhjpp9","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","group","family"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"\"22 acres of camp sites\" in Dunlap: 30 sites (1 tent-only group site, 25 RV/tent sites, 4 lodging yurts); sites #3-#5 with water and sewer hookups; \"restrooms with showers\" in a geodesic dome, laundry, a seasonal pond; \"about 25mi from sequoia and Kings Canyon right off the Highway 180\" (host)."},{"name":"Camp Hye Sierra, Dunlap","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/california-camp-hye-sierra-xryhve96","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","family"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"A 160-acre retreat \"about 35 miles east of Fresno\", \"perfect for reflection and fellowship\": 4 RV/tent sites (\"no electrical hookup\"), four cabin units (\"MATTRESSES ONLY. YOU NEED TO BRING YOUR OWN SLEEPING BAGS AND PILLOWS\"), two stocked lakes, canoes and paddle boats; \"within a 30-minute drive from the Grant Grove Visitor Center\" (host)."},{"name":"Bella Brooke Cafe and Gena''s Sierra Inn, Dunlap","source":"https://bellabrookecafe.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in (\"No Reservations Needed\"); motel booking via the own website","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","stay"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"\"37692 E Kings Canyon Road, Dunlap CA 93621\": \"aged steaks, country sized burgers, hearty pastas, strong coffee, and local micro brew beer\"; \"7am - 10pm Everyday. No Reservations Needed. Open To Everyone.\" Motel cabins and chalets; about 20 minutes from the Big Stump Entrance and \"less than 5 minutes from the last gas and groceries before entering the National Parks.\""},{"name":"Clingan''s Junction cabins and coffee, Squaw Valley","source":"https://www.clingansjunction.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"own website / phone 559-790-6432","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","stay"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"\"Cozy cabins + coffee, conveniently located 19 miles from Sequoia and King''s Canyon National Park\": four remodeled cabins (Mimi''s Cottage, Sweet Mountain Cabin, Cozy Mountain Cabin, Clingan''s Junction Cottage) and an on-site coffee shop; 559-790-6432. The site also says \"just 16.2 miles from the entrance\"."},{"name":"Marriott Hotel Visalia","source":"https://hotelguides.com/attraction-maps/california/map-hotels-near-kings-canyon-national-park-ca.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":39,"blurb":"Listed by HotelGuides at \"300 South Court, Visalia, CA 93291\", \"46 miles from Kings Canyon Park North Entrance\", described as \"Upper-upscale, smoke-free, full-service, downtown hotel\". Marriott''s own page was not fetched (brand sites return 403), so nothing else is stated here. Visalia is the Sequoia-side gateway; the 46 miles is HotelGuides'' figure."},{"name":"Hampton Inn Visalia","source":"https://hotelguides.com/attraction-maps/california/map-hotels-near-kings-canyon-national-park-ca.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"hilton.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":40,"blurb":"Listed by HotelGuides at \"4747 West Noble Avenue, Visalia, CA 93277\", 49 miles from Kings Canyon Park North Entrance. Hilton''s own page was not fetched, so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Holiday Inn Express Visalia","source":"https://hotelguides.com/attraction-maps/california/map-hotels-near-kings-canyon-national-park-ca.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior"],"booking_route":"ihg.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":41,"blurb":"Listed by HotelGuides at \"5625 West Cypress Avenue, Visalia, CA 93277\", 49 miles from Kings Canyon Park North Entrance. IHG''s own page was not fetched, so nothing else about the property is stated here."}],"faq":[{"q":"Do you have to pay to enter Kings Canyon National Park?","a":"Yes. \"Pay your entrance fee at park entrance stations.\" A 7-day pass for US residents is \"$35\" per single vehicle, \"$30\" per motorcycle and \"$20\" per individual; non-residents pay \"$35 +$100/non-resident\" per vehicle, the per-person fee charged \"for each non-resident visitor 16 years or older\". Annual and lifetime passes cover the fee.","source":"https://nps.gov/seki/learn/news/upload/Trip_Planner_2026_Spring_2026-03-19_01_for_web_508.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp in Kings Canyon National Park?","a":"Yes, in designated campgrounds: Azalea, Sunset and Crystal Springs at Grant Grove and Sentinel, Sheep Creek, Moraine and Canyon View group at Cedar Grove. \"Reservations are required except for Azalea Campground\"; sites hold up to six people at \"$32 per night\", and \"Roadside camping is not permitted in the parks.\"","source":"https://nps.gov/seki/learn/news/upload/Trip_Planner_2026_Spring_2026-03-19_01_for_web_508.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Kings Canyon National Park?","a":"Only in developed areas, not on trails: \"Pets are not permitted on any trails in the parks. Pets in designated areas must be kept on a maximum 6-foot (1.8 m) leash at all times.\" John Muir Lodge offers \"Dog-friendly accommodations\" at a \"$25 per night pet fee\" (visitsequoia.com).","source":"https://nps.gov/seki/learn/news/upload/Trip_Planner_2026_Spring_2026-03-19_01_for_web_508.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Do you need a permit for Kings Canyon National Park?","a":"For overnight wilderness trips, yes. \"Reservations can be made up to six months in advance of your trip, and are released daily at 7:00 AM Pacific Standard Time\"; in the 2026 quota season (\"May 22, 2026 - September 26, 2026\") the fee is \"$15 each trip plus $5 per person\". Day visitors pay the entrance fee.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/wilderness_permits.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can you stay in Kings Canyon National Park?","a":"Three lodges run by the park concessioner: John Muir Lodge (\"36 rooms in Kings Canyon National Park\"), Grant Grove Cabins (\"both timber and tent cabin styles\") and Cedar Grove Lodge (\"21 guest rooms\", May through mid-October), booked at visitsequoia.com or (866) 807-3598 - plus the seven NPS campgrounds.","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/stay/lodging/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can you eat in Kings Canyon National Park?","a":"Grant Grove Restaurant serves breakfast 7-10 a.m. and lunch/dinner 11:30 a.m.-8 p.m. \"overlooking Bradley Meadow\", with a seasonal walk-up courtyard; in Cedar Grove the Grill offers \"light meals and snacks\" on a balcony \"overlooking the Kings River\". The Grant Grove and Cedar Grove markets sell groceries and picnic supplies.","source":"https://www.visitsequoia.com/kings-canyon-dining/grant-grove-restaurant/","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim in Kings Canyon National Park?","a":"The NPS warns: \"Drowning is the primary cause of death in the parks. Rocks near rivers are slippery. Most drowning victims did not intend to swim. Currents are strong, fast, and very cold. Do not leave children unattended anywhere near a river edge.\" For Cedar Grove it flags \"Severe drowning danger\", particularly spring through early summer (nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cedar-grove.htm).","source":"https://nps.gov/seki/learn/news/upload/Trip_Planner_2026_Spring_2026-03-19_01_for_web_508.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you hunt in Kings Canyon National Park?","a":"No: \"Hunting and trapping are illegal in the parks.\" In the neighbouring Sequoia National Forest hunting is allowed \"Only seasonally with a license\" (California Department of Fish and Wildlife, 559-243-4005).","source":"https://nps.gov/seki/learn/news/upload/Trip_Planner_2026_Spring_2026-03-19_01_for_web_508.pdf","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Kings Canyon a national park?","a":"Yes. \"The Grant Grove area was originally General Grant National Park, created in 1890 to protect giant sequoias from logging.\" Today, per the NPS planner, \"This is not one, but two national parks—Sequoia and Kings Canyon—managed by the National Park Service as one unit.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/grant-grove.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Kings Canyon National Park open in winter?","a":"Grant Grove stays reachable, with \"deep snow and cold temperatures in winter\"; Cedar Grove \"typically operates from May through early to mid-November\" (nps.gov/seki/planyourvisit/cedar-grove.htm). The spring 2026 planner listed \"Highway 180 to Cedar Grove (opens late April)\" and \"Panoramic Point Road\" as closed, and chains or traction devices can be required. Road conditions: (559) 565-3341.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/seki/grant-grove.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Kings Canyon National Park: General Grant Tree & Cedar Grove | TravelWell","meta_description":"The General Grant Tree, Zumwalt Meadow and Mist Falls, seven campgrounds, three lodges, 2026 entrance fees, and glamping and RV stays on Highway 180.","slug":"kings-canyon-national-park-california","primary_keyword":"Kings Canyon National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Kings Canyon National Park Cedar Grove"}}'::jsonb, 93),
  ('pinnacles-california', '12A', 'Pinnacles National Park', 'United States', 'Talus caves, volcanic spires and California condors', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Central Coast & the Sierra', '{"hiking","wildlife","adventure","family","parks"}', '{"rugged","dramatic","adventurous","remote"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"High Peaks to Bear Gulch Loop","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/trails.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail; park entrance fee applies","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"\"6.7 miles round trip, 4 to 5 hours\", elevation \"1,425 feet\", rated \"Strenuous\": \"ascending through wildflower-filled meadows in spring, then descending through shady woodlands\"."},{"name":"Bear Gulch Cave","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/cavestatus.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","family","wildlife","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail; check cave status before going","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"A talus cave sheltering \"Townsend''s big-eared bats\", whose maternity colony is \"the largest one between San Francisco and Mexico\"; \"Mid-May - Mid-July: The entire cave is closed to protect the bats during the pupping season\". The Lower Cave can be explored \"without needing to turn back, even when the upper section is closed.\" Lower and Upper Cave both \"OPEN\" on the day read."},{"name":"California condors of the High Peaks","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/bird-watching.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","hiking","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - self-guided wildlife viewing","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"\"In 2003, Pinnacles became a release site for the California Condor.\" The NPS birding page: \"Arrive early to spot California Condors roosting before they take flight\"; condors carry \"vinyl ID tags\" with colors indicating age, and sightings can be reported to the Pinnacles Condor Program at 831-389-4486, extension 4276."},{"name":"Balconies Cave from Old Pinnacles Trailhead","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/trails.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"\"5.3 miles round trip, 3 to 5 hours\", no elevation gain, rated \"Moderate\"; Balconies Cave \"OPEN\" on the day read. The NPS advises: \"pack a flashlight or headlamp. Cave sections can be dark\"."},{"name":"Moses Spring to Rim Trail Loop","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/trails.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"\"2.2 miles round trip, 1 to 1-1/2 hours\", elevation \"500 feet\", rated \"Moderate\"; the NPS names Moses Spring Trail among its kid-friendly trails."},{"name":"Condor Gulch to High Peaks Loop","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/trails.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"\"5.3 miles round trip, 3 to 5 hours\", elevation \"1,300 feet\", rated \"Strenuous\"."},{"name":"Pinnacles Campground","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/camp.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","group","motoring"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov (campgrounds/234015) or (877) 444-6777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"East side, open year-round: \"family and group tent sites, as well as RV sites with electric hookups\" (120v/30-amp); \"Each tent and group site is equipped with a picnic table and fire ring\"; \"Coin-operated showers, a dump station\"; \"The pool is typically open from mid-April through the end of September\". The concessioner counts \"134 campsites\". \"Generators are not allowed at any time in any site\"; \"First come, first served sites are NOT available at this location\"."},{"name":"Pinnacles Campground tent cabins","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/lodging.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","family","romance"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov or (831) 200-1722","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"\"canvas-sided tent cabins that provide a rustic lodging experience\", sleeping up to four, \"open year-round\"; the only roofed stay in the park - \"There is no lodging available within Pinnacles National Park\". Tent cabin check-in 3pm, checkout 11am (Recreation.gov)."},{"name":"Prewett Point Trail","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"\"0.9 miles round trip, 1/2 to 1 hour\", elevation \"70 feet\", rated \"Easy\" (nps.gov/pinn trails page); \"This newly constructed accessible trail is less than a mile long and offers panoramic views.\""},{"name":"Bench Trail accessible section","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"\"A recently hardened and graded section of the Bench Trail is now accessible for visitors using wheelchairs.\""},{"name":"Rock climbing on volcanic breccia","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/climb.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - self-guided; no permit is mentioned on the climbing FAQ","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"\"The rock formations here are composed of volcanic breccia, which can be loose in places, increasing the potential for rockfall.\" Topropes \"are perfect for beginners\"; multi-pitch climbs on Machete Ridge for the experienced; \"During the nesting season from January through July, certain climbing areas may be temporarily closed\". The NPS names no commercial guide and points climbers to Friends of Pinnacles."},{"name":"Chalone Peak Trail","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/trails.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"\"9 miles round trip, 3 to 5 hours\", elevation \"2,040 feet\", rated \"Strenuous\"."},{"name":"Juniper Canyon Loop","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/trails.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - park trail","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"\"4.3 miles round trip, 2 to 3 hours\", elevation \"1,215 feet\", rated \"Strenuous\"."},{"name":"Junior Ranger Program and ranger nature walks","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/learn/kidsyouth/index.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed - park programme","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"\"The Junior Ranger Program at Pinnacles National Park is a fun and educational way for kids to explore and learn about the park''s unique ecosystems, wildlife, and geological features.\" \"Join a park ranger for a fun nature walk!\" \"Older kids and school groups can participate in service learning projects throughout the year.\""},{"name":"Group campsites at Pinnacles Campground","source":"https://www.visitpinnacles.com/camping","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"Recreation.gov (campgrounds/234015) or (877) 444-6777","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"\"Group sites: 20 people, five vehicles max\" (concessioner); \"Group sites can be reserved up to 12 months in advance\" (NPS). Non-commercial groups of 16+ passengers pay \"$15.00\" per person entrance, children 15 and under exempt."},{"name":"Birding the 181 documented species","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/bird-watching.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","senior","hiking"],"booking_route":"none needed - self-guided","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"\"181 documented species\"; the spires host \"Turkey Vultures, Peregrine Falcons, and Prairie Falcons\" plus migrants like \"Blue-Gray Gnatcatchers and various warbler species\"; \"The rocky spires and monoliths provide ideal vantage points for bird watching.\""},{"name":"Pinnacles Campground Store","source":"https://www.visitpinnacles.com/camping","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","hiking"],"booking_route":"walk-in store","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat","shop","gear"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"Run by Pinnacles Recreation Company, \"a small, family-owned business\" and the park''s concessioner: \"A general store with basic foods and camping supplies is located on-site\" (Recreation.gov); open \"9:30am-5pm daily\". \"There are no restaurants or grocery stores within Pinnacles National Park.\""},{"name":"East side weekend shuttle","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"none stated - boards at the campground","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["move"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"Runs \"seasonally in late winter and spring from 8 am to 5:30 pm Friday through Sunday\" from the campground; it had concluded for the season on the day read. Pets are not allowed on shuttle buses."},{"name":"Mission Nuestra Señora de la Soledad","source":"https://soledadmission.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","pilgrimage","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed - walk-in during open hours","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"\"Founded in 1791 by Father Fermin Lasuen\", \"the thirteenth mission to be founded in California\"; 36641 Fort Romie Road, Soledad; open \"10AM-4PM Tuesday-Sunday. Closed on Mondays\"; self-guided tours through the volunteer-staffed shop."},{"name":"Paicines Ranch","source":"https://www.paicinesranch.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wellness","group","culinary","wildlife","romance"],"booking_route":"own website booking (rooms and cottages)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","activities"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"\"Nestled in the heart of San Benito County\": a working ranch of about 7,000 acres of rangeland, 550 acres of row crops and 25 acres of vineyard, all certified organic; rooms and cottages to book, birding under dark skies, \"Weddings, Retreats & Gatherings\". 831-628-0288."},{"name":"Calera Wine Company","source":"https://www.calerawine.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","culinary","romance"],"booking_route":"own website booking (tours and tastings)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"11300 Cienega Road, Hollister: Robert Parker Wine Advocate calls it \"one of the most compelling Pinot Noir specialists of not only the New World, but of Planet Earth\"; founder Josh Jensen planted on remote limestone slopes atop Mount Harlan. Tastings booked through its tours and tastings page; (831) 637-9170."},{"name":"Eden Rift Vineyards","source":"https://www.edenrift.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","romance","adventure"],"booking_route":"own website reservation (edenrift.com/reservation)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"10034 Cienega Road, Hollister: tastings \"Thursday-Sunday from 12pm to 5pm\" on the Dickinson House lawn, ATV vineyard tours, and helicopter tours through Specialized Aviation; (831) 636-1991."},{"name":"DeRose Winery","source":"http://derosewine.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","culinary"],"booking_route":"walk-in tasting room; phone 831-636-9143","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"9970 Cienega Road, Hollister: \"a land rich in winemaking history\" with dry-farmed vineyards; tasting \"Monday-Friday, 11:00 am - 5:00 pm Saturday and Sunday, 11:00 am - 4:00 pm\"; 831-636-9143."},{"name":"Léal Vineyards","source":"https://www.liveloveleal.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wine","romance","group"],"booking_route":"own website reservation system","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"300 Maranatha Drive, Hollister: in operation \"since 1998\", calls itself \"one of the most sought-after wineries in California\" and runs all-inclusive event services; 1.831.636.1023."},{"name":"Jardines de San Juan","source":"https://www.jardinesrestaurant.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family","culture"],"booking_route":"phone (831) 623-4466 or info@jardinessjb.com","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"115 3rd St, San Juan Bautista: established in 1977 by Alicia and Manuel Santana and still family-owned; open 7 days, Sunday-Thursday 11 am - 8 pm, Friday and Saturday 11 am - 9 pm; (831) 623-4466."},{"name":"Food & Wine at The Overlook, Paicines Ranch","source":"https://www.paicinesranch.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","wine","romance"],"booking_route":"own website (ranch calendar); 831-628-0288","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"Farm-to-table dinners \"featuring ingredients from local farmers and the ranch''s own livestock\"; Thursday lunches 11:30 AM-1:30 PM; seasonal dinners and concerts on the ranch calendar."},{"name":"Fairfield Inn & Suites Hollister","source":"https://www.americansouthwest.net/california/hotels/hollister.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"marriott.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_pct_low":8,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"Listed by American Southwest at \"390 Gateway Drive, Hollister, CA 95023\" with \"77 guest rooms & suites\", \"a fitness center, and indoor pool\"; \"Pinnacles National Park, is 30 miles south.\" Marriott''s own page was not fetched (brand sites return 403 to this agent), so nothing else about the property is stated here."},{"name":"Holiday Inn Express & Suites Hollister","source":"https://www.americansouthwest.net/california/hotels/hollister.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","senior","group"],"booking_route":"ihg.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"Listed by American Southwest at \"391 Gateway Drive, Hollister, CA 95023\": \"93 room/suite\", \"24 hour fitness & business centers, an indoor pool\", opened in late 2022. IHG''s own page was not fetched (brand sites return 403 to this agent)."},{"name":"SureStay Hotel by Best Western Hollister","source":"https://www.americansouthwest.net/california/hotels/hollister.html","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","motoring"],"booking_route":"bestwestern.com (brand booking; not fetched)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"Listed by American Southwest at \"660 San Felipe Road, Hollister, CA 95023\": \"42 room, exterior corridor\", at the junction of highways 25 and 156."},{"name":"Pinnacles View - 2 mi from Park","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/california-pinnacles-view-2-mi-from-park-lz9hxeod","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","wine","hiking"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"Soledad: \"Park your fully self-contained camping vehicle beside our organic vineyard, just 2 miles from the Westside entrance of Pinnacles National Park.\" 4 RV-only sites for self-contained rigs under 30 feet; \"No tent or car camping is allowed\"; \"we do NOT have services on site\"; no campfires, no pets."},{"name":"Song of the Ancients: Dark Sky Camping","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/california-song-of-the-ancients-dark-sky-camping-near-pinnacles-xryh0xkm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","family","wildlife"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"Paicines, Diablo Range: 4 RV/tent sites on 40 acres, \"dark skies, ancient blue oaks, forest bathing\"; fire pits with grills, flush toilets, outdoor hot shower, potable water; sites take 12 to 20 people; no hookups and \"no stores nearby\". Hipcamp lists it 14 miles from the park."},{"name":"Camp Carmel Valley - Glamping","source":"https://www.hipcamp.com/en-US/land/california-camp-carmel-valley-glamping-zwjhrenx","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","family","group"],"booking_route":"Hipcamp","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"\"Located on 115 acres historic boys and girls summer camp complete with pool, tennis, and hiking in Carmel Valley, CA\": Sunset and Solstice/Sunrise cabins, safari tents at Rustic Grove Camp and a bunk room; breakfast included with all glamping stays; weekend campfires, yoga and archery. Hipcamp lists it 28 miles from the park."},{"name":"Hollister Hills State Vehicular Recreation Area","source":"https://ohv.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=1179","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","motoring","family"],"booking_route":"first-come, first-serve at the kiosk; a few sites online","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay","activities"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"7800 Cienega Road, about 5 miles south of Hollister in the Gabilan Mountains: \"Camping $10 per vehicle per night\"; Lower Ranch and Upper Ranch campsites \"remain first-come, first-serve\"; only two remote Hudner Ranch sites and the Lower Ranch ADA sites reserve online. An off-highway-vehicle park."},{"name":"Pinnacles National Park Foundation","source":"https://pinnaclesfoundation.org/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","group"],"booking_route":"none needed - volunteering and donations via the website","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"A \"501(c)(3) non-profit organization dedicated to supporting Pinnacles National Park\", funding \"high-priority programs and projects unfunded by park budgets\" - habitat restoration, wildlife conservation, cultural resources, volunteering. PO Box 2080, Hollister; 831.320.1570."},{"name":"Water for the trail - one liter per hour","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/basicinfo.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":35,"blurb":"NPS: \"Water is not available on the trails, so bring enough for your entire trip\"; \"carry and drink at least one liter of water per person per hour\" of hiking."},{"name":"Flashlight or headlamp for the talus caves","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","hiking","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to blackdiamondequipment.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":7,"commission_pct_high":7,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":36,"blurb":"NPS: \"Bring a Flashlight: Navigating these caves in the dark without proper lighting can be dangerous.\" The trails page: \"pack a flashlight or headlamp. Cave sections can be dark\"."},{"name":"Sun protection - hat, sunscreen, light clothing","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":37,"blurb":"NPS: \"Wear light-colored clothing, a hat, and sunscreen to shield yourself from direct sunlight.\" \"Staying hydrated and protecting yourself from the sun is critical.\""},{"name":"Sturdy boots with ankle support","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":38,"blurb":"NPS: \"Sturdy shoes or boots with ankle support and good tread are essential.\""},{"name":"Binoculars for condor watching","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/bird-watching.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","senior","family"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to rei.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":39,"blurb":"NPS birding page: \"Binoculars: A pair in the 7-10 power range is ideal.\""},{"name":"Climbing helmet for loose breccia","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/climbfaq.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate referral to blackdiamondequipment.com (AvantLink)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":7,"commission_pct_high":7,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":40,"blurb":"NPS climbing FAQ: \"wear a helmet, especially on the West Side where loose rocks are common\"; use \"brown or gray webbing\" for anchors and \"Chalk balls\" instead of loose chalk."}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Pinnacles National Park free?","a":"No. The NPS lists a private-vehicle fee of \"$30.00\", valid 1-7 days for up to 15 passengers; \"$15.00\" per person on foot or bicycle (under 16 free); motorcycles \"$25.00\". America the Beautiful passes, including the \"$20.00\" Senior Annual, are accepted. The park does not accept cash.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/fees.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp at Pinnacles National Park?","a":"Yes, at Pinnacles Campground on the east side, which has \"Tent, group, and RV sites\" plus tent cabins. \"Tent and RV sites can be reserved up to 6 months in advance. Group sites can be reserved up to 12 months in advance\", through recreation.gov or (877) 444-6777.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/camp.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you drive through Pinnacles National Park?","a":"No: \"There is no road connecting the East and West entrances of the park.\" The shortest drive between them goes through King City on Highway 101.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/directions.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What is the best time to visit Pinnacles National Park?","a":"The NPS: \"Spring and fall are typically the most pleasant weather for hiking and visiting the park.\" In July and August \"Daytime temperatures... frequently exceed 100°F (38°C)\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/weather.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you bring dogs to Pinnacles National Park?","a":"Only to some areas. Pets are allowed in \"Picnic areas, Campground, Parking lots, Paved roads\" on a six-foot leash, and are not allowed on \"All park trails, Shuttle buses, Park buildings.\"","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/pets.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"When did Pinnacles become a national park?","a":"\"On January 10, 2013 President Barack Obama signed legislation passed by Congress that redesignated the monument as a National Park.\" It had been a national monument since 1908.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/learn/historyculture/present-day.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can you see condors in Pinnacles National Park?","a":"The NPS points to the High Peaks - \"Arrive early to spot California Condors roosting before they take flight\" - and says the Balconies Trail may also offer sightings. It recommends binoculars \"in the 7-10 power range\".","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/bird-watching.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where can you stay in Pinnacles National Park?","a":"\"There is no lodging available within Pinnacles National Park\" apart from the campground, which offers tent sites, RV sites and \"canvas-sided tent cabins\" sleeping up to four, \"open year-round\". The NPS points to chambers of commerce in San Benito County, King City, Soledad and the Salinas Valley for town lodging.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/lodging.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Which is better, the east or west entrance of Pinnacles National Park?","a":"They serve different visits. The east side has the Pinnacles Visitor Center, the campground and \"24-hour access to trails\"; the west side has the Pinnacles Visitor Contact Station and a day-use gate \"open from 7:30 am to 8:00 pm\". No road connects the two.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/hours.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What should you wear to Pinnacles National Park?","a":"The NPS: \"Wear light-colored clothing, a hat, and sunscreen to shield yourself from direct sunlight\"; \"Sturdy shoes or boots with ankle support and good tread are essential\"; and bring a flashlight for the caves.","source":"https://www.nps.gov/pinn/planyourvisit/safety.htm","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Pinnacles National Park: High Peaks, Talus Caves & Condors | TravelWell","meta_description":"Strenuous High Peaks loops, Bear Gulch and Balconies talus caves, California condors since 2003, east-side camping with tent cabins, and where to stay nearby.","slug":"pinnacles-national-park-california","primary_keyword":"Pinnacles National Park","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Pinnacles National Park High Peaks"}}'::jsonb, 94),
  ('point-lobos-california', '12A', 'Point Lobos State Natural Reserve', 'United States', 'Cypress headlands and kelp-forest coves', 'future', 'verified', 'mountainValley', 'Central Coast & the Sierra', '{"hiking","diveglobal","wildlife","family","senior","parks"}', '{"dramatic","coastal","serene","wild"}', '{}', null, null, '{"safety":{"posture":"book-freely","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","verified":"2026-10-08"},"jewels":[{"name":"Cypress Grove Trail","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/AccessibleFeatures/Details/571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","senior","wildlife"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond the reserve entry fee ($10.00 per vehicle)","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":1,"blurb":"Leaves from the Information Station; California State Parks rates it \"accessible for 0.25 mile\" with excellent views of the cove, with accessible parking in the Cypress Grove area and an accessible restroom at Cypress Grove."},{"name":"Diving and snorkelling at Whalers and Bluefish Coves","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=28353","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["diveglobal","wildlife","ocean","adventure"],"booking_route":"state dive reservation online from the Point Lobos SCUBA Diving page, or (831) 624-8413","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":2,"blurb":"\"Diving is permitted only at Whalers and Bluefish Coves\" in the Point Lobos State Marine Reserve: \"70 foot-high kelp forests\" with \"lingcod, rockfish, harbor seals, sea otters, sea stars, and more\"; ten teams of two a day; proof of certification and a reservation required; weekend/holiday $30 and weekday $20 per pair plus processing fee; \"Snorkeling is NOT permitted at China Cove or Gibson Beach.\""},{"name":"Sand Hill Trail (Sea Lion Point)","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/AccessibleFeatures/Details/571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","hiking","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond the reserve entry fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":3,"blurb":"A \"paved accessible loop trail about 0.4 mile long\" leading to views of the cove \"and perhaps the occasional otter and/or sea lion\", with accessible parking at the Sea Lion Point lot."},{"name":"Bird Island Trail","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/AccessibleFeatures/Details/571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond the reserve entry fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":4,"blurb":"From the Bird Island trailhead, \"0.52 miles\" on an \"aggregate, rock, & wood\" surface; the Bird Island picnic area has \"four accessible tables including accessible parking and restroom\". Gibson Beach, the South Shore Trail and the South Plateau Trail leave from the same trailhead."},{"name":"Point Lobos docent-guided walks","source":"https://docents.plsnr.org/publicwalks","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["senior","hiking","culture","family"],"booking_route":"listed on the docents'' public walks page; booking terms not stated","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":5,"blurb":"Public walks by the reserve''s docents, mostly 10:00-10:30am with some at 1:00pm, from the Information Station or Whalers Cabin: the \"Cypress Grove Treasures Walk\" on \"cultural history and the natural wonders\", an \"Easy-Access Adventure Walk\" for \"visitors of all abilities\" on the Sea Lion Point trail, a General Walk, and \"The Women Who Shaped and Saved Point Lobos Walk\". No cost or booking terms were stated on the page."},{"name":"Whalers Cabin Museum","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","senior","family"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond the reserve entry fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":6,"blurb":"Open \"9:00am to 5:00pm (As staffing permits)\" at Whalers Cove; the state describes the reserve as \"once the site of countless industrial activities, from whaling operations and gravel quarries to the largest abalone cannery on the West Coast.\""},{"name":"Point Lobos Summer Adventures","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=27276","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","wildlife","hiking"],"booking_route":"registration with the Program Director, ashley.wemp@parks.ca.gov, (831) 884-2957","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":7,"blurb":"\"an outdoor day camp for kids and teenagers\", based at Point Lobos with visits to other local parks: hiking, nature art, habitat restoration, and \"whale watching, kayaking and on other cool field trips\". 2026 sessions June 15-26 ($600), July 6-17 ($600), July 20-29 ($450); registration first-come, first-served."},{"name":"Kayak and stand-up paddleboard launch at Whalers Cove","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=28353","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","ocean","wildlife"],"booking_route":"state reservation from the Point Lobos SCUBA Diving page, or (831) 624-8413","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":8,"blurb":"\"Kayaks and Stand-Up Paddleboards are $10 to launch\"; \"There is a limit of four Kayak/ SUPs per day\", entering only at the Whalers Cove dive ramp; reserved \"in the same way as dive reservations\"; \"CA State Parks does not rent any kayaks, stand up paddleboards, or dive equipment to park visitors.\""},{"name":"Carmelo Meadow and Granite Point Trails","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/AccessibleFeatures/Details/571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond the reserve entry fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":9,"blurb":"Carmelo Meadow runs \"0.25 miles each way\" from the entry station and links to the Granite Point Trail, \"0.36 miles each way\", both compacted soil \"generally flat at less than 5% slopes\"; the route \"winds through native Monterey Pine forest and terminates at Whalers Cove.\""},{"name":"Lace Lichen Trail","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/AccessibleFeatures/Details/571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond the reserve entry fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":10,"blurb":"\"0.75 miles each way\" through native forest on compacted soil, rated accessible by California State Parks; one of the three trails the state lists from the reserve entrance, with the Carmelo Meadow and South Shore trails."},{"name":"Point Lobos trail network","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=29389","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","wildlife","family"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond the reserve entry fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":11,"blurb":"The state''s Point Lobos Hiking Trails page names the Perimeter Trail and the trails from five trailheads: the Reserve Entrance (Carmelo Meadow, South Shore, Lace Lichen), the Information Station (Cypress Grove, North Shore, Sea Lion Point / Sand Hill, South Shore), Bird Island (Bird Island, Gibson Beach, South Shore, South Plateau), Whalers Cove (Granite Point, North Shore, Cabin) and Piney Woods (Pine Ridge, South Shore)."},{"name":"Picnic areas at Whalers Cove, Piney Woods and Bird Island","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/AccessibleFeatures/Details/571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","group","senior"],"booking_route":"none needed beyond the reserve entry fee","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":12,"blurb":"Three picnic areas: Whalers Cove \"one accessible table on firm surface\", Piney Woods an accessible table on dirt, and Bird Island \"four accessible tables including accessible parking and restroom\". Reserve rules: \"Smoking and fires of all types are prohibited; this includes small cookstoves\" and \"Alcohol consumption is not allowed anywhere within the reserve.\""},{"name":"Group, tour-bus and school-field-trip entry","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","senior","family"],"booking_route":"special event permit via the reserve''s Special Events Coordinator, 831-624-3407; school groups via the School Group Coordinator, 831-625-1470","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":13,"blurb":"\"ALL tours and buses MUST have a special event permit to enter the reserve. ALL school groups MUST have a reservation to enter the reserve.\" Bus (10-24 passengers) $50.00 and Bus (25+ passengers) $100.00, \"PERMIT REQUIRED\"; vehicles over 21 ft are not allowed, except \"school field trip buses with a permit for drop off and pick up of students.\" Special Events Coordinator (tours, beach weddings, films) 831-624-3407."},{"name":"Layers for the coastal fog: what the state says to expect","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","family","senior"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":14,"blurb":"Under \"Seasons/Climate/Recommended Clothing\" the state writes: \"Fair sunny days, occasional winter rains, and dry summers, moderated by fog from July through September characterize the central California coastal climate.\" Rain shell, warm layer and walking shoes for a fog-and-sun day, bought before the trip."},{"name":"Snorkel and dive kit for Whalers Cove: bring your own","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=28353","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["diveglobal","ocean","adventure"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip - or hired from a Monterey dive shop","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":15,"blurb":"\"CA State Parks does not rent any kayaks, stand up paddleboards, or dive equipment to park visitors. There are a variety of shops that rent gear to the public in Monterey.\" \"All SCUBA divers must have a device capable of maintaining positive buoyancy\"; \"All snorkelers need a buddy in order to enter the water.\""},{"name":"Binoculars for watching marine mammals at a distance","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=28353","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["wildlife","family","senior"],"booking_route":"affiliate link to the retailer (AvantLink); bought before the trip","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"affiliate","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":5,"commission_pct_high":5,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["gear"],"draw_rank":16,"blurb":"The state quotes NOAA Fisheries: \"recommended distances of at least 100 YARDS (300 feet) for whales, and 50 YARDS (150 feet) for dolphins, seals, sea lions, and turtles\"; and \"If you approach seals, otters, whales, or seabirds and notice they are alerting to your presence then you are too close.\""},{"name":"8-Day Yosemite, Sequoia & California Coast Adventure (Southwest Adventure Tours, on TourRadar)","source":"https://www.tourradar.com/t/104098","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["group","senior","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"TourRadar (tourradar.com/t/104098)","commission_status":"commissioned","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","commission_pct_low":7,"commission_pct_high":7,"commission_basis":"published","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":17,"blurb":"A multi-day guided group tour, San Francisco round trip, 8 days, 4-14 participants, ages 8+, from EUR 4,707 per person; Day 6 \"Cambria to Monterey\" includes a \"Scenic drive along Pacific Coast Highway (Highway 1)\" and \"Visit Point Lobos State Natural Reserve\". TourRadar''s listing: \"Ancient Sequoia groves give way to coastal paths at Point Lobos State Park and along Moonstone Beach in Cambria\"."},{"name":"Carmel-by-the-Sea","source":"https://www.carmelcalifornia.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","romance","culinary","wine"],"booking_route":"none needed - a public town","commission_status":"none","tier_absent_reason":"not-sold","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":18,"blurb":"The gateway village three miles north of the reserve: \"this one-square mile, fairytale village full of inspired restaurants, wine tasting, boutique shops, art galleries, a white-sand beach, and stunning scenery—all within walking distance from your hotel or inn.\""},{"name":"Monterey Bay Aquarium","source":"https://www.montereybayaquarium.org/visit/admission-tickets","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["family","wildlife","senior","ocean"],"booking_route":"own website tickets","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":19,"blurb":"886 Cannery Row, Monterey; a nonprofit whose mission is \"to inspire conservation of the ocean\". Adult $65 (ages 18-69), Youth $50 (5-17), Senior $50 (70+), free for ages 4 and under; \"Purchase your tickets in advance for a smooth entry process.\""},{"name":"Carmel Mission Basilica","source":"https://carmelmission.org/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culture","pilgrimage","senior"],"booking_route":"visit details on the mission''s Plan Your Visit pages (admission terms not read); 831.624.1271","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["activities"],"draw_rank":20,"blurb":"3080 Rio Road, Carmel: \"A PLACE OF WORSHIP, EDUCATION, HISTORY, AND ART\" with museums and \"the extraordinary collection art and religious artifacts\"; \"Two centuries ago, the Carmel Mission was in ruins.\" Sunday Masses 9:00 and 11:00 a.m. in the Basilica."},{"name":"Aquarius Dive Shop, Monterey","source":"https://aquariusdivers.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["diveglobal","ocean","adventure"],"booking_route":"own website booking (DiveShop360) or 831-375-1933","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","activities"],"draw_rank":21,"blurb":"2040 Del Monte Ave., Monterey: \"Established in 1970, Aquarius Dive Shop is Monterey Bay''s premier PADI 5-Star Instructor Development Center\", with a heated training pool, \"a full service rental department\", and guided shore dives - \"We offer shore dives every day.\" Mon-Thu 9am-6pm, Fri-Sun 7am-7pm. The reserve itself rents no dive equipment."},{"name":"Monterey Bay Kayaks","source":"https://www.montereybaykayaks.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["adventure","wildlife","family","ocean"],"booking_route":"own website booking or (831) 373-5357","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"operator","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["gear","activities"],"draw_rank":22,"blurb":"Kayak and stand-up paddleboard rentals, guided tours and classes \"in the Monterey Bay National Marine Sanctuary, exciting harbor and Cannery Row shoreline with sea otters, seals, sealions, kelp beds and more\", plus Elkhorn Slough; stores selling \"Kayaks - new and used, Gear, Clothing & More\"; open daily 9-5, (831) 373-5357."},{"name":"Carmel by the River RV Resort","source":"https://www.carmelrv.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["motoring","family"],"booking_route":"online via CamperClick (app.camperclick.com/p/carmelrv) or +1 (831) 624-9329","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":23,"blurb":"27680 Schulte Rd., Carmel: 35 back-in sites, all with water, sewer, 30 or 50 amp electric, WiFi and cable TV; pet-friendly; propane fire-pit rentals; \"8.6 miles to Point Lobos State Natural Reserve\". No tent camping."},{"name":"Ventana Campground, Big Sur","source":"http://www.ventanacamping.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["glamping","family","hiking"],"booking_route":"hyatt.com booking link from the campground site, or 855-391-8683","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":24,"blurb":"48123 Highway 1, Big Sur, \"30 miles south of Carmel\": a tent-only campground on 40 acres in a redwood canyon with glamping tents (\"A More Refined Way to Connect with Nature\"), two modern bath houses, picnic table and fire ring per site; \"We cannot accommodate RVs\"; up to 2 dogs per site on leash; a three-night minimum in the busy summer season. Bookings run through Hyatt."},{"name":"Pfeiffer Big Sur State Park campground","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=570","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["hiking","group","family"],"booking_route":"ReserveCalifornia","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":25,"blurb":"\"Big Sur''s largest campground\", 26 miles south of Carmel: tent, en route, group and hike-and-bike sites; RVs to 32 ft and trailers to 27 ft, with a dump station; Big Sur Lodge has \"61 guest rooms\". ⚠️ The state lists the park as closed due to the Timber Fire as of September 15, 2026."},{"name":"Alila Ventana Big Sur","source":"https://www.ventanabigsur.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","wellness","senior"],"booking_route":"own website booking or 800.628.6500","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":26,"blurb":"48123 Highway One, Big Sur, an Alila resort in the Hyatt family: \"Ventana''s 54 rooms and suites are arranged around our 160-acre property in secluded groupings\"; stays include dining, non-alcoholic drinks, wellness programming and valet; restaurants The Sur House, The Glass House and SurStream; glamping on the same estate."},{"name":"Carmel Valley Ranch","source":"https://carmelvalleyranch.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["golf","family","wellness","romance","wine"],"booking_route":"own website booking or 855.687.7262","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","commission_basis":"benchmark","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":27,"blurb":"One Old Ranch Road, Carmel, in The Unbound Collection by Hyatt: \"LUXURY CALIFORNIA RESORT ON 500 ACRES\" with all-suite accommodation, pools, Spa Aiyana, its own vineyard and \"The only Pete Dye-designed bentgrass golf course\" (page text truncated there); \"Romantics and families alike find action and fun\"."},{"name":"La Playa Hotel, Carmel-by-the-Sea","source":"https://www.carmelcalifornia.com/hotels-and-inns-in-carmel/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["romance","senior"],"booking_route":"direct booking per the Carmel tourism listing; (831) 293-6100","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"hotel","tier_absent_reason":"not-established","wells":["stay"],"draw_rank":28,"blurb":"Listed by Carmel''s official tourism site among Carmel hotels and inns, (831) 293-6100, \"Book Direct\", with a listed \"$1,149.00 Average Nightly Rate\". The hotel''s own page was not read."},{"name":"Hog''s Breath Inn","source":"https://hogsbreathinn.net/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture","romance"],"booking_route":"own website reservations or 831-625-1044","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":29,"blurb":"547 San Carlos St., Carmel-by-the-Sea: \"Founded in 1970 by Clint Eastwood\", USDA Prime steak and sustainable seafood \"beside the warmth of our famous fireplaces and heated outdoor patio\"; the patio is dog-friendly; lunch daily from 11:00 a.m."},{"name":"Rio Grill","source":"https://www.riogrill.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"reservations 831.625.5436 (OpenTable linked)","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":30,"blurb":"101 Crossroads Blvd, Carmel, at \"The Crossroads at Highway 1 and Rio Road — the gateway to Big Sur\": California Fusion since 1983, \"Originally opened in 1983 as a coastal sister to Mustard''s Grill\"; Mon-Thu 11:30 AM-8:00 PM, Fri-Sat to 9:00 PM."},{"name":"Little Napoli","source":"https://chefpepe.com/restaurants/little-napoli/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","romance","family"],"booking_route":"online reservations or 831.626.6335","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":31,"blurb":"Corner of Dolores St. & 7th St. in the 1928 El Paseo Building, Carmel-by-the-Sea: \"Opened in 1990\", Chef Pèpe''s southern Italian; \"Best Italian Restaurant – 2025 Golden Pine Cones\"; dinner nightly 4pm-9:00pm; \"Reservations are recommended but not required\"; cashless; pet-friendly courtyard."},{"name":"Vesuvio","source":"https://chefpepe.com/restaurants/vesuvio/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"Tock or 831.625.1766; walk-ins welcome","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":32,"blurb":"543 6th Ave, Carmel-by-the-Sea, across from Devendorf Park: \"Wood-fired pizza. Two bars, one on the roof. Open nightly at four.\" \"Walk-ins welcome. The rooftop, the full Downstairs Bar and a few dining tables are always held for you.\""},{"name":"Cultura Comida y Bebida","source":"https://www.culturacarmel.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","culture"],"booking_route":"online reservations or (831) 250-7005","commission_status":"unknown","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":33,"blurb":"Dolores Street between 5th & 6th Avenue, in the Su Vecino Courtyard, Carmel-by-the-Sea: \"Celebrating The Culture of Oaxaca, Mexico\"; menu \"all made from scratch\" from fresh local ingredients; a mezcal library; (831) 250-7005."},{"name":"Carmel Belle","source":"https://www.carmelbelle.com/","accessed":"2026-10-03","si":["culinary","family"],"booking_route":"walk-in; online ordering on own website","commission_status":"none","commission":"venue","tier_absent_reason":"does-not-compete","wells":["eat"],"draw_rank":34,"blurb":"Dowd Building #110, Ocean Avenue & San Carlos, Carmel-by-the-Sea: breakfast, lunch and dinner from \"the freshest local ingredients from Monterey County\"; open daily 8:00am-5:30pm; 831-624-1600."}],"faq":[{"q":"Do you need tickets for Point Lobos State Natural Reserve?","a":"There is no timed ticket for a car; entry is paid per vehicle: \"Vehicle $10.00 Senior $9.00 Disabled (with Discount Pass) $5.00\". Buses pay $50.00 or $100.00 with a permit, and \"ALL tours and buses MUST have a special event permit to enter the reserve. ALL school groups MUST have a reservation to enter the reserve.\" Divers and snorkellers need a separate reservation.","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Point Lobos State Natural Reserve free?","a":"No. California State Parks lists \"Vehicle Day Use: $10.00\", with a $9.00 senior rate and $5.00 with the Disabled Discount Pass, and notes that \"Special rates may apply for peak season, high demand holiday periods, and during weekends.\" The reserve accepts state passes including the California Explorer and Golden Poppy annual passes.","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What are the hours at Point Lobos State Natural Reserve?","a":"\"RESERVE HOURS 8 am - 7 pm No Vehicles or Pedestrians may enter the Reserve after 6:30 pm.\" The Information Station and the Whalers Cabin Museum open \"9:00am to 5:00pm (As staffing permits)\".","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you camp at Point Lobos State Natural Reserve?","a":"No. \"No Camping. The reserve is strictly a Day Use facility and all visitors must exit by closing time.\" Smoking and fires \"of all types are prohibited; this includes small cookstoves.\"","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Does Point Lobos State Natural Reserve allow dogs?","a":"No. \"Dogs are not allowed anywhere within the reserve and cannot be left inside parked vehicles.\"","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Can you swim at Point Lobos State Natural Reserve?","a":"The state''s page covers diving and snorkelling, not swimming: \"The diving area is limited to Whalers and Bluefish Coves. All other areas of the Reserve are closed to diving and aquatic activity. Snorkeling is NOT permitted at China Cove or Gibson Beach.\" Diving and snorkelling need a reservation, and \"All snorkelers need a buddy in order to enter the water.\"","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=28353","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where is Point Lobos State Natural Reserve?","a":"\"The reserve is located on the central coast of California in Monterey County. The entrance is located three miles south of Carmel on Highway 1.\" Mailing address: Route 1 Box 62, Carmel, CA 93923.","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"What are the trails at Point Lobos State Natural Reserve?","a":"California State Parks groups them by trailhead: from the Reserve Entrance, Carmelo Meadow, South Shore and Lace Lichen; from the Information Station, Cypress Grove, North Shore, Sea Lion Point / Sand Hill and South Shore; from Bird Island, Bird Island, Gibson Beach, South Shore and South Plateau; from Whalers Cove, Granite Point, North Shore and Cabin; from Piney Woods, Pine Ridge and South Shore; plus the Perimeter Trail.","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=29389","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Is Point Lobos State Natural Reserve good with kids?","a":"The reserve runs Point Lobos Summer Adventures, \"an outdoor day camp for kids and teenagers\" with hiking, nature art, habitat restoration and \"whale watching, kayaking and on other cool field trips\"; 2026 sessions were June 15-26 and July 6-17 at $600 and July 20-29 at $450, registration first-come, first-served.","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=27276","accessed":"2026-10-03"},{"q":"Where do you park at Point Lobos State Natural Reserve?","a":"Inside the reserve, at a $10.00 vehicle fee; \"any vehicle (commercial, motorhome, live-in van, etc.) over 21 ft long is not allowed to drive or park within Point Lobos State Natural Reserve.\" Accessible parking is at the entrance, the Sea Lion Point lot, the Cypress Grove area and each trailhead (California State Parks accessible features page).","source":"https://www.parks.ca.gov/?page_id=571","accessed":"2026-10-03"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Point Lobos State Natural Reserve, CA: Trails, Diving & Carmel | TravelWell","meta_description":"Day-use reserve 3 miles south of Carmel: cypress trails, sea lions, kelp-forest diving at Whalers Cove by reservation, $10 per car, no dogs, no camping.","slug":"point-lobos-state-natural-reserve-california","primary_keyword":"Point Lobos State Natural Reserve","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination"},"hero":{"query":"Point Lobos State Natural Reserve cypress cove"}}'::jsonb, 95)
